        "id": 1013984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-14T18:20:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Compiling a pattern is an expensive operation, and here you\u0027re dynamically creating one for each locale - can\u0027t you just do a direct string comparison?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 113,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 113,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "fe5f1831b401c540c7ca3d46b8b65b978033ac85",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "61658199_b3b9655d",
        "filename": "core/java/com/android/internal/app/LocalePicker.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 113,
      "author": {
        "id": 1682499
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-07-14T21:02:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it is an expensive operation, but the pattern is compiled once per getting a list of supported locales or update locales call, not for each locale. The above mentioned operations are themselves rarely called, so I think it is safe to keep it as is. Using string comparison doesn\u0027t allow to reasonably cover all the necessary use cases.\n\nAlternatively, I could cache the pattern to a static field (given the current class design), but it is generally not really a good thing to do (unless there\u0027s a strong reason), plus it would make the method much harder to test (without extra injection points).",
      "parentUuid": "1597b740_4b5d41db",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 113,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 113,
        "endChar": 73
      },
